PS5 VRR: HDMI VRR with an open-ended VRRmax, and the HF-SCDB

VRRmax 0 in the HDMI Forum VSDB means the sink sets no upper limit (VRR up to the highest
refresh rate it accepts); it was read as "no HDMI VRR range". A Panasonic OLED announces
VRRmin 48, VRRmax 0, so it fell through to its FreeSync block, and since VRR is offered only
with HDMI VRR it was reported as not VRR capable. VRRmax 0 now takes the FreeSync maximum when
there is one, else 120 Hz. FreeSync-only displays (no HDMI VRR) are still refused.
Also read the same fields from the HF-SCDB (extended tag 0x79), which newer TVs use instead
of the VSDB.
---

--- a/drivers/ps5/hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/ps5/hdmi.c
@@ -1395,6 +1395,14 @@
 	}
 	kfree(e);
 
+	/*
+	 * VRRmax 0 means the sink sets no upper limit: VRR goes up to the highest refresh
+	 * rate it accepts. Take that from the FreeSync range when there is one, else 120 Hz,
+	 * the highest rate this HDMI chip drives.
+	 */
+	if (hf_min >= 1 && hf_max == 0)
+		hf_max = amd_max > hf_min + 10 ? amd_max : 120;
+
 	if (hf_min >= 1 && hf_max > hf_min + 10) {
 		*min_hz = hf_min; *max_hz = hf_max; *src = "HDMI VRR range";
 	} else if (amd_min >= 1 && amd_max > amd_min + 10) {
